[agent:result] Usage: hops files upload [OPTIONS] LOCAL_PATH REMOTE_PATH
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Upload a local file to HopsFS.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   ``REMOTE_PATH`` is the destination path (``cp``/``scp``-style), not the
[agent:result]   parent directory. When its basename matches the local file's basename the
[agent:result]   parent is used as the SDK's ``upload_path``; otherwise the remote path is
[agent:result]   passed through unchanged and the SDK treats it as a directory (file lands
[agent:result]   under ``REMOTE_PATH/<local basename>``).
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Args:     ctx: Click context.     local_path: Local source file.
[agent:result]   remote_path: HopsFS destination path.     overwrite: Pass-through to the
[agent:result]   SDK's upload call.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Options:
[agent:result]   --overwrite             Overwrite an existing remote file.
[agent:result]   --json                  Output as JSON (machine-readable; for LLMs and
[agent:result]                           scripts).
[agent:result]   --verify / --no-verify  Verify the Hopsworks TLS certificate; --no-verify
[agent:result]                           skips verification for self-signed / IP-SAN-
[agent:result]                           mismatched certs.
[agent:result]   -h, --help              Show this message and exit.
