[agent] The full FTI pipeline is complete on the platform, and every artifact is verified through platform read paths. Held-out RMSE is **1.770 µg/m³**, well under the 2.178 target.
[agent] What was built (all executed as a Hopsworks Python job in the `pandas-training-pipeline` environment — nothing computed locally):
[agent] - **Feature group `airq754fa9`** (v1) — 979 history rows with the weather columns plus engineered signals: `pm25_lag1`/`pm25_lag2`, rolling means `pm25_roll3`/`pm25_roll7` (shifted to avoid leakage), and seasonal calendar features (`doy_sin`, `doy_cos`, `month`). Verified via Trino: 979 rows.
[agent] - **Training dataset `airqtd754fa9`** — a feature view over the FG with `pm25` as label, materialized as a train/test split (758 train / 221 test rows, read back platform-side).
[agent] - **Model `airqmodel754fa9`** (v1) — a `HistGradientBoostingRegressor` trained on the split, registered in the model registry with metrics `rmse=1.7701, mae=1.3202, r2=0.5514`, then refit on the full history for the final forecaster. It uses only features available at forecast time (lag-1 + weather + calendar), since the sparse forecast days make multi-day rolling values uncomputable at inference.
[agent] - **Predictions `airqpred754fa9`** (v1, online-enabled) — all 90 rows of `forecast_days.csv` with primary key `date` and column `pm25_pred`. Verified offline via Trino (90 rows, 2025-04-17 → 2026-05-30) and via an online-store read from a platform job (`ONLINE_ROWS=90`), so it's available for low-latency lookup as well.
[agent] Two environment notes: the local sandbox only reaches the cluster through the HTTP proxy (I had to strip `NO_PROXY` on each CLI call), so direct ArrowFlight/MySQL reads from this machine fail — I verified offline data through `hops sql` (Trino, `delta` catalog) and online data through a platform job instead. Also, `hops td list` errors locally with a client/backend version mismatch (`'FeatureView' object has no attribute '_get_training_dataset_schema'`), but the training dataset itself reads back fine via the SDK on-platform.
